From 3debafa480b60a0d58fc2b126e9e21d8ee3c0499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FK-16 candidate <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:26:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] FK-16 (0.3.32 candidate 4): gate proves the published
 artifact; refusal reasons kept

From the independent review of 4c19dfa:
- Compatibility tests run against the packed @feltdb/feltkit's dist (../src points at it), not src/.
- Both packages packed and inspected (lockstep pin); uncommitted release manifests may differ from the
  commit in version strings only.
- publish-packages publishes exactly the checked tarballs (FELTKIT_RELEASE_ARTIFACT_DIR) and, before
  moving latest, requires the registry to serve their exact sha512.
- E401/E403 classified as refused, not unreachable.
- Policy delegation records keep a refusal's reason (not installed vs. unregistered agent).
- A configuration-state refusal on a person's connection points to readiness generally; docs say it
  applies to any caller. CHANGELOG states the empty-url development fallback and the gate's limits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HaRh2AeLLCdd3FVn7atuCR
